  TypeDecl
    LineComment "// A nominal type over a builtin base is a wrapper: a value of the base type flows"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// into it, the way an integer literal has always flowed into `type Level = int8`."
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// Before F-1 this adaptation existed for integers alone, so a string, bool, or"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// collection wrapper could not be written with a literal. This example folds that"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// generalization end to end — a string base, a refinement, and union tagging."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// A bare string adapts to the nominal type that wraps it. The const folds to the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// string, carried at the nominal type Tag."
    Newline "\n"
